  "description": "Retrospective application for the conversion of the garage to facilitate habitable accommodation and a front porch extension and proposed alterations to the front porch fenestration, removal of the rear entrance door and change of use of the dwelling (C3(b)) to a children's care home for up to 5 children (C2)",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The plans lack consistency and clarity,&nbsp; failing to demonstrate that the accommodation would be suitable for 5 children and overnight staff. The limited number of bedrooms would require room sharing, which is not considered appropriate in a care setting where unrelated children should have individual space, thus representing a poor quality of accommodation. No provision has been made for sleep-in staff, further undermining the quality of accommodation.&nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)&nbsp;",
    "The proposed development represents intensification of the site. Due to the significant number of residents and care staff, the proposal would result in a harmful loss of residential amenity, increasing comings and goings, noise and general disturbance for neighbouring occupiers.&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)Policies&nbsp;GG3, D6 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy DMSI 3 of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "3.&nbsp;The proposed development fails to demonstrate&nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore likely to add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&nbsp;which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision: National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024) Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DMT1 and&nbsp;DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
